      "visible": true,
      "showLabel": false,
      "data": {
        "title": "An Event Handler Binds an Event to a Method",
        "statement": "An Event Handler should be the complete, inspectable binding between one Event and one Method. When the Event occurs, the Method executes with the complete occurrence. The Method owns every decision and effect; Twilite supplies delivery safeguards and live diagnostics.",
        "status": "revised",
        "confidence": "plausible",
        "notes": "This idea defines the handler behavior contract. The Event remains a first-class occurrence, while the Handler binds that Event to a Method without requiring a separate Subscription node for the common case.",
        "definitionKey": "idea",
