      "data": {
        "view": {
          "intent": "node",
          "payload": "node.web.detail"
        },
        "semanticLevel": "detail",
        "content": {
          "kind": "markdown",
          "value": "# What an Event Handler Node Should Do\n\nAn Event Handler is a readable binding: **one Event invokes one Method**.\n\nEvery matching occurrence invokes the Method. The Method receives the occurrence and owns decisions, executable logic, mutation authority, and declared effects.\n\nTwilite supplies delivery safeguards and live diagnostics; durable run history requires an explicit logging reaction. Several Events may share one reaction through separate Event Handlers that reference the same Method."
        },
        "interfaceContract": {
          "version": 1,
          "ownsContent": true,
          "surfaceDelegation": true
        },
        "identity": {
          "graphId": "event-handler-behavior"
        }
      }
    },
