      "visible": true,
      "showLabel": false,
      "data": {
        "title": "How a delivered handler runs and reports",
        "findings": "Delivery hands the handler's code to the script runner with the occurrence id, root occurrence id, event key, payload, delivery id, and the allowMutations and dry-run flags. If action.methodNodeId names a Method, the Method's source runs instead of the handler's own. Delivery is refused when a required bridge runtime grant is missing. The handler node shows last-run status held in component state, and failures also raise a warning notification. Mutation permission is one boolean (allowMutations); in the code reviewed, nothing states which nodes a handler intends to change.",
        "sourceUrl": "github://TwiliteLLC/twilite/components/GraphEditor/GraphEditor.js",
        "sourceType": "runtime-inspection",
        "definitionKey": "idea-research",
